    "probe_text": "Confirmed directly: nothing in `src/` implements the `addOwner` operation \u2014 it appears only in the OpenAPI spec (`openapi.yml:69`) and the mapper's `toOwner` signature. Here's the honest answer.\n\n## `POST /api/owners` is not actually implemented\n\nAs the code stands, **there is no working create-owner endpoint**, so there is no runtime create flow to enumerate. The route is declared only by the OpenAPI-generated interface `OwnersApi.addOwner(...)`, whose default method returns `501 NOT_IMPLEMENTED`. No `@RestController` implements it:\n\n- The only Owner controller is `OwnerRestControllerV2`, which handles **GET** (`listOwnersPage`) only \u2014 no POST.\n- Grep confirms no class implements `OwnersApi`; `OwnerFieldsDto` is referenced only by the mapper.\n\nSo a `POST /api/owners` request would return **501** (or 404), and nothing downstream \u2014 no service check, no repository lookup, no event \u2014 ever runs.\n\n## What *would* apply, in order, if a request reached the generated stub\n\n**1. Bean Validation on the request body** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`), the only validation layer that actually exists:\n\n| Field | Constraints |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `firstName` | `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern(\"^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$\")` |\n| `lastName` | `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern(\"^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$\")` |\n| `address` | `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,255)`, `@Pattern(\"(?s).*\\S.*\")` |\n| `city` | `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,80)`, `@Pattern(\"(?s).*\\S.*\")` |\n| `telephone` | `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,20)` |\n| `email` | `@Size(max=255)` (optional) |\n| `registrationDate` | `@Valid` (optional) |\n| `sharesHousehold`, `postcode` | none (optional) |\n\nNo class-level or custom validators apply to Owner (the only `ConstraintValidator` in the repo, `PetAgeValidator`, is for pets).\n\n**2. Nothing else.** There is no create logic to run after validation:\n- **No service checks** \u2014 `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner()` is just `ownerRepository.save(owner)`. No telephone normalization, no duplicate check, no default `registrationDate`, no capacity/rate limits.\n- **No repository guards** \u2014 `OwnerRepository` has no `existsBy\u2026`/`countBy\u2026` methods.\n- **No entity lifecycle callbacks** \u2014 no `@PrePersist`/`@PreUpdate`/`@EntityListeners` on `Owner`, `Person`, or `BaseEntity`.\n- **No events, listeners, email, or audit logging.**\n- **Mapping** would be a plain MapStruct field copy (`OwnerMapper.toOwner`, ignoring `id`/`pets`) with no normalization or defaults.\n\n## Worth flagging\n\nThe OpenAPI docs on `OwnerFieldsDto` and the integration test `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests` assert a much richer create flow \u2014 E.164 telephone normalization, duplicate-telephone \u2192 **409**, city-at-capacity \u2192 **409**, daily-limit \u2192 **429**, a derived `displayName`, a default `registrationDate`. **None of that logic exists in `src/main`.** So either an `OwnerRestControllerV1` implementing `OwnersApi` is missing/unwritten, or it was removed \u2014 those tests would currently fail against this code.\n\nIf you'd like, I can point you at exactly where a V1 controller would need to be added to satisfy that contract."
